# literal_translation = Setting out from thence, covered in thick mist, by night they walked uttering a very beautiful voice, singing of aegis-bearing Zeus and queen Argive Hera, treading with golden sandals, and the flashing-eyed daughter of aegis-bearing Zeus, Athena, and Phoebus Apollo and archer Artemis, and earth-holding, earth-shaking Poseidon, and reverend Themis and glancing Aphrodite, and golden-crowned Hebe and fair Dione, and Leto and Iapetus and crooked-counselling Cronus, and Eos and great Helios and bright Selene, and Gaia and great Ocean and black Night, and the sacred race of other immortals that ever are.

