# literal_translation = Verily first of all Chaos came to be, but then broad-bosomed Gaia, ever the sure seat of all [immortals who hold the peak of snowy Olympus], and misty Tartarus in a recess of broad-wayed earth, and Eros, who is fairiest among immortal gods, limb-loosing, and subdues the mind and shrewd counsel in the breasts of all gods and all men.

