# literal_translation = And to Nereus in the barren sea were born most lovely goddess-children from rich-haired Doris, daughter of Oceanus, the perfect river: Ploto, Eucrante, Sao, Amphitrite, Eudora, Thetis, Galene, Glauke, Cymothoe, Speo, Thoe, lovely Halie, Pasithea, Erato, rosy-armed Eunice, graceful Melite, Eulimene, Agave, Doto, Proto, Pherusa, Dynamene, Nesaea, Actaea, Protomedea, Doris, Panopea, fair Galatea, lovely Hippothoe, rosy-armed Hipponoe, and Cymodoce who easily calms the waves on the misty sea and the blasts of raging winds with Cymatolege and fair-ankled Amphitrite, Cymo, Eione, well-crowned Halimede, laughter-loving Glauconome, Pontoporea, Liagora, Evagora, Laomedea, Polynoe, Autonoe, Lysianassa, Evarne lovely in form and blameless in appearance, Psamathe graceful in body, divine Menippe, Neso, Eupompe, Themisto, Pronoe, and Nemertes, who has the mind of her immortal father.


