# literal_translation = And to Phorcys Ceto again bore the fair-cheeked Graeae, grey from birth, whom indeed immortal gods and men who walk on the ground call Graeae—well-robed Pemphredo and saffron-robed Enyo—and the Gorgons, who dwell beyond glorious Oceanus in the borderland towards Night, where are the clear-voiced Hesperides: Sthenno and Euryale and Medusa who suffered woeful things.

