# literal_translation = Him indeed then the might of Heracles slew beside his shambling cattle in sea-girt Erytheia, on that very day when he drove the broad-browed cattle to holy Tiryns, having crossed the ferry of Oceanus and slain Orthos and the herdsman Eurytion in the gloomy steading beyond glorious Oceanus.

