# literal_translation = And she bore a holy race of daughters, who across the earth nurture young men with lord Apollo and the Rivers, and they have this portion from Zeus: Peitho, and Admete, and Ianthe, and Electra, and Doris, and Prymno, and godlike Urania, and Hippo, and Clymene, and Rhodeia, and Callirhoe, and Zeuxo, and Clytie, and Idyia, and Pasithoe, and Plexaure, and Galaxaure, and lovely Dione, and Melobosis, and Phoe, and comely Polydora, and Cerceis lovely in form, and ox-eyed Pluto, and Perseis, and Ianira, and Acaste, and Xanthe, and lovely Petraea, and Menestho, and Europa, and Metis, and Eurynome, and saffron-robed Telesto, and Chryseis, and Asia, and charming Calypso, and Eudora, and Tyche, and Amphiro, and Ocyrhoe, and Styx, who indeed is the foremost of them all.

