# literal_translation = For thus advised imperishable Styx, an Oceanid, on that day when the Olympian Lightener called all the immortal gods to long Olympus, and said that whoever of the gods should fight with him against the Titans, he would not strip anyone of his privileges, but each would hold the honor which he had before among the immortal gods; and he said that whoever was unhonored by Cronus and unrewarded would enter upon honor and privileges, as is right.

