# literal_translation = And Rhea, subdued by Cronus, bore glorious children: Hestia, Demeter, and golden-sandaled Hera, and mighty Hades, who inhabits halls beneath the earth having a pitiless heart, and the loud-crashing Earth-shaker, and wise Zeus, father of gods and also of men, beneath whose thunder even the broad earth is shaken.

