# literal_translation = That bird then Heracles, the valiant son of beautiful-ankled Alcmene, slew, and warded off the evil plague from the son of Iapetus and freed him from sufferings, not against the will of Olympian Zeus ruling on high, so that the fame of Thebes-born Heracles might be still greater than before upon the bounteous earth.

