# literal_translation = For long they fought having toil that grieves the heart, both Titan gods and as many as were born from Cronus, against one another through mighty battles—on the one hand the lordly Titans from lofty Othrys, and on the other hand the gods from Olympus, givers of good things, whom lovely-haired Rhea bore lying with Cronus.

