# literal_translation = And there in order are the sources and ends of all—of gloomy earth and misty Tartarus and unharvested sea and starry heaven—grievous, mouldy, which even gods abhor, a great gulf; nor would one reach the ground for a whole full year, if once one were inside the gates, but storm after grievous storm would carry him hither and thither onward;

